From: OpenEmbedded <oe@oe-alliance.org>
Date: 2026-05-02
Subject: [PATCH] mod_openssl: fix build with OpenSSL 4.0

OpenSSL 4.0 made ASN1 string types opaque. Use accessor functions
instead of direct struct member access.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: OpenEmbedded <oe@oe-alliance.org>

diff -urN a/src/mod_openssl.c b/src/mod_openssl.c
--- a/src/mod_openssl.c	2026-05-02 18:13:23.201376046 +0200
+++ b/src/mod_openssl.c	2026-05-02 18:13:23.222811817 +0200
@@ -4860,8 +4860,8 @@
             if (prelen+len >= sizeof(key)) continue;
             memcpy(key+prelen, xobjsn, len); /*(not '\0'-terminated)*/
             http_header_env_set(r, key, prelen+len,
-                                (const char*)X509_NAME_ENTRY_get_data(xe)->data,
-                                X509_NAME_ENTRY_get_data(xe)->length);
+                                (const char*)ASN1_STRING_get0_data(X509_NAME_ENTRY_get_data(xe)),
+                                ASN1_STRING_length(X509_NAME_ENTRY_get_data(xe)));
         }
     }
 }
